Sure, here's a function to initialize GPIO for the ESP32 using ESP-IDF:

```c
#include "driver/gpio.h"

void initialize_gpio(void) {
    // Set GPIO 2 as an output
    gpio_config_t io_conf;
    io_conf.intr_type = GPIO_INTR_DISABLE;
    io_conf.mode = GPIO_MODE_OUTPUT;
    io_conf.pin_bit_mask = (1ULL << 2);
    io_conf.pull_down_en = 0;
    io_conf.pull_up_en = 0;
    gpio_config(&io_conf);
}
```

This function configures GPIO 2 as an output pin. You can adjust the pin number and other settings as needed for your specific application.
